1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,158
For thirty years,

2
00:00:01,158 --> 00:00:03,408
the coolest cars in the world had

3
00:00:03,408 --> 00:00:04,771
headlights that hid.

4
00:00:04,951 --> 00:00:07,194
The Lamborghini Countach,

5
00:00:07,194 --> 00:00:08,988
the Ferrari F forty,

6
00:00:08,988 --> 00:00:10,693
the Mazda M X five,

7
00:00:10,693 --> 00:00:11,859
the Corvette.

8
00:00:12,039 --> 00:00:12,983
Press a button,

9
00:00:12,983 --> 00:00:14,997
and the lights flipped up out of

10
00:00:14,997 --> 00:00:16,822
the bonnet like opening eyes.

11
00:00:17,002 --> 00:00:19,404
Then, in two thousand four,

12
00:00:19,404 --> 00:00:21,716
the last ones disappeared.

13
00:00:21,896 --> 00:00:25,188
Today, ten parts of car headlights,

14
00:00:25,188 --> 00:00:28,573
and the engineering story of why pop

15
00:00:28,573 --> 00:00:29,419
ups died.

16
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:31,929
Headlights look like a simple part.

17
00:00:32,109 --> 00:00:35,113
But they sit at the meeting point

18
00:00:35,113 --> 00:00:36,569
of laws, safety,

19
00:00:36,569 --> 00:00:39,481
aerodynamics and new technology.

20
00:00:39,661 --> 00:00:42,066
Every time one of those changed,

21
00:00:42,066 --> 00:00:43,794
headlights changed too.

22
00:00:43,974 --> 00:00:46,473
The pop up headlight was born from

23
00:00:46,473 --> 00:00:47,722
one set of rules,

24
00:00:47,722 --> 00:00:49,338
and killed by another.

25
00:00:49,689 --> 00:00:52,881
As always, every fact here comes from

26
00:00:52,881 --> 00:00:54,175
a named source,

27
00:00:54,175 --> 00:00:59,093
safety regulations, car makers and automotive references,

28
00:00:59,093 --> 00:01:01,682
all listed in the description.

29
00:01:01,862 --> 00:01:03,847
Let's start with the pop ups.

30
00:01:04,197 --> 00:01:06,515
Why did so many sports cars have

31
00:01:06,515 --> 00:01:08,399
headlights that popped up?

32
00:01:08,579 --> 00:01:11,465
Because designers wanted a very low,

33
00:01:11,465 --> 00:01:14,431
pointed nose, to cut through the air.

34
00:01:14,611 --> 00:01:16,469
But in the United States,

35
00:01:16,469 --> 00:01:19,145
the law required headlights to be at

36
00:01:19,145 --> 00:01:22,935
least about fifty-six centimetres above the ground.

37
00:01:23,115 --> 00:01:24,525
On a low sports car,

38
00:01:24,525 --> 00:01:26,710
the nose was simply too low for

39
00:01:26,710 --> 00:01:27,062
that.

40
00:01:27,413 --> 00:01:29,755
The solution was to hide the lights

41
00:01:29,755 --> 00:01:30,960
inside the bonnet,

42
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:33,101
and raise them only when needed.

43
00:01:33,281 --> 00:01:35,068
With the lights down,

44
00:01:35,068 --> 00:01:37,705
the nose stayed low and smooth.

45
00:01:37,885 --> 00:01:39,028
With the lights up,

46
00:01:39,028 --> 00:01:40,532
they met the height rule.

47
00:01:40,712 --> 00:01:42,713
A car like the Mazda M X

48
00:01:42,713 --> 00:01:45,632
five or the Lotus Esprit could have

49
00:01:45,632 --> 00:01:48,467
both a wedge shaped nose and legal

50
00:01:48,467 --> 00:01:49,385
headlights.

51
00:01:49,735 --> 00:01:52,733
The flip up movement also became part

52
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:53,624
of the fun.

53
00:01:53,804 --> 00:01:56,115
Owners would wink the lights at each

54
00:01:56,115 --> 00:01:58,298
other, and the cars seemed to come

55
00:01:58,298 --> 00:01:59,261
alive at night.

56
00:01:59,441 --> 00:02:01,886
For a generation of car fans,

57
00:02:01,886 --> 00:02:05,090
pop up headlights became the symbol of

58
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:06,186
a sports car,

59
00:02:06,186 --> 00:02:08,463
as much as a loud engine or

60
00:02:08,463 --> 00:02:09,390
a big wing.

61
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:12,330
Why did pop up headlights disappear?

62
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:15,528
Several reasons arrived at the same time.

63
00:02:15,708 --> 00:02:17,368
The first was safety.

64
00:02:17,548 --> 00:02:20,864
New rules in Europe aimed to protect

65
00:02:20,864 --> 00:02:23,075
pedestrians hit by cars.

66
00:02:23,255 --> 00:02:26,257
A raised headlight has hard edges and

67
00:02:26,257 --> 00:02:29,422
corners, right where a person's legs or

68
00:02:29,422 --> 00:02:31,289
body would hit the car.

69
00:02:31,469 --> 00:02:33,735
Designers had to make the front of

70
00:02:33,735 --> 00:02:35,602
the car smoother and softer.

71
00:02:35,952 --> 00:02:38,959
The second reason was weight and cost.

72
00:02:39,139 --> 00:02:42,130
Each pop up headlight needs a motor,

73
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:44,042
a mechanism and wiring,

74
00:02:44,042 --> 00:02:45,454
and it can break.

75
00:02:45,634 --> 00:02:48,084
The third was aerodynamics.

76
00:02:48,264 --> 00:02:49,980
When the lights are up,

77
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:52,592
the clean low nose suddenly has two

78
00:02:52,592 --> 00:02:54,831
bricks sticking into the wind,

79
00:02:54,831 --> 00:02:57,592
adding drag exactly when you drive at

80
00:02:57,592 --> 00:02:58,040
night.

81
00:02:58,390 --> 00:03:01,315
The last reason was new technology.

82
00:03:01,495 --> 00:03:04,831
Smaller, brighter lights could be placed low

83
00:03:04,831 --> 00:03:07,181
in a smooth nose and still meet

84
00:03:07,181 --> 00:03:07,939
the rules.

85
00:03:08,119 --> 00:03:11,340
The Chevrolet Corvette and the Lotus Esprit

86
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:14,111
kept pop ups until two thousand four,

87
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,909
and then they were gone.

88
00:03:16,089 --> 00:03:19,189
The problem they solved no longer existed.

89
00:03:19,539 --> 00:03:22,339
Why did old American cars all have

90
00:03:22,339 --> 00:03:25,715
the same round or rectangular headlights?

91
00:03:25,895 --> 00:03:27,497
Because of a rule.

92
00:03:27,677 --> 00:03:30,868
From the end of the nineteen thirties,

93
00:03:30,868 --> 00:03:34,899
US law required standard sealed beam headlights.

94
00:03:35,079 --> 00:03:38,267
The lamp, the reflector and the glass

95
00:03:38,267 --> 00:03:40,076
were one sealed unit,

96
00:03:40,076 --> 00:03:42,920
made in only a few standard sizes

97
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:43,867
and shapes.

98
00:03:44,218 --> 00:03:46,005
The idea was practical.

99
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:47,493
If a light failed,

100
00:03:47,493 --> 00:03:49,383
you could buy a new one at

101
00:03:49,383 --> 00:03:51,127
any shop in the country,

102
00:03:51,127 --> 00:03:52,362
and it would fit.

103
00:03:52,542 --> 00:03:54,597
But it also froze design.

104
00:03:54,777 --> 00:03:56,862
Every car had to use the same

105
00:03:56,862 --> 00:03:59,739
few lamps, and designers could not shape

106
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:01,824
the lights to match the body.

107
00:04:02,004 --> 00:04:04,551
That is one reason pop ups became

108
00:04:04,551 --> 00:04:07,869
popular, because they hid the ugly standard

109
00:04:07,869 --> 00:04:08,332
lamps.

110
00:04:08,681 --> 00:04:11,632
The rule changed in the nineteen eighties,

111
00:04:11,632 --> 00:04:14,864
when the United States allowed headlights with

112
00:04:14,864 --> 00:04:18,306
replaceable bulbs, shaped freely by the designer.

113
00:04:18,486 --> 00:04:20,276
Lights could now be low,

114
00:04:20,276 --> 00:04:22,364
wide and curved to the body.

115
00:04:22,544 --> 00:04:25,427
That change, more than anything else,

116
00:04:25,427 --> 00:04:28,155
opened the door to the smooth faces

117
00:04:28,155 --> 00:04:29,324
of modern cars.

118
00:04:29,675 --> 00:04:32,404
Why is there gas inside a halogen

119
00:04:32,404 --> 00:04:33,645
headlight bulb?

120
00:04:33,825 --> 00:04:36,338
A normal bulb has a thin metal

121
00:04:36,338 --> 00:04:37,761
wire, a filament,

122
00:04:37,761 --> 00:04:40,106
that glows when it gets hot.

123
00:04:40,286 --> 00:04:43,684
Over time, metal from the filament evaporates

124
00:04:43,684 --> 00:04:45,421
and blackens the glass,

125
00:04:45,421 --> 00:04:48,291
and the filament gets thinner until it

126
00:04:48,291 --> 00:04:48,819
breaks.

127
00:04:48,999 --> 00:04:52,349
A halogen bulb adds a small amount

128
00:04:52,349 --> 00:04:54,910
of a gas such as iodine or

129
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:55,698
bromine.

130
00:04:56,049 --> 00:04:58,626
That gas creates a chemical cycle.

131
00:04:58,806 --> 00:05:01,922
The evaporated metal combines with the gas,

132
00:05:01,922 --> 00:05:04,168
and later lands back on the hot

133
00:05:04,168 --> 00:05:04,820
filament.

134
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,477
The glass stays clear,

135
00:05:06,477 --> 00:05:08,624
and the filament can run hotter,

136
00:05:08,624 --> 00:05:11,443
which makes the light brighter and whiter.

137
00:05:11,623 --> 00:05:14,002
That is why halogen bulbs are made

138
00:05:14,002 --> 00:05:15,122
of quartz glass,

139
00:05:15,122 --> 00:05:16,941
which can handle the heat.

140
00:05:17,291 --> 00:05:20,681
Halogen bulbs became the standard in car

141
00:05:20,681 --> 00:05:22,631
headlights for decades.

142
00:05:22,811 --> 00:05:24,274
They are cheap and simple.

143
00:05:24,454 --> 00:05:27,089
But a hot quartz bulb is sensitive.

144
00:05:27,269 --> 00:05:29,892
The oil from a fingertip can create

145
00:05:29,892 --> 00:05:31,916
a hot spot on the glass and

146
00:05:31,916 --> 00:05:33,339
make it fail early,

147
00:05:33,339 --> 00:05:36,187
which is why mechanics never touch the

148
00:05:36,187 --> 00:05:37,985
glass with bare fingers.

149
00:05:38,336 --> 00:05:41,435
Why are some headlights bright and slightly

150
00:05:41,435 --> 00:05:41,795
blue?

151
00:05:41,975 --> 00:05:43,901
They are xenon lamps,

152
00:05:43,901 --> 00:05:47,293
also called high intensity discharge.

153
00:05:47,473 --> 00:05:49,703
Instead of a glowing wire,

154
00:05:49,703 --> 00:05:53,135
they create a small electric arc between

155
00:05:53,135 --> 00:05:56,910
two electrodes, inside a capsule filled with

156
00:05:56,910 --> 00:05:59,141
xenon gas and metal salts.

157
00:05:59,321 --> 00:06:01,572
The arc produces a very bright,

158
00:06:01,572 --> 00:06:02,444
white light.

159
00:06:02,794 --> 00:06:06,213
Xenon lamps produce about three times as

160
00:06:06,213 --> 00:06:08,606
much light as halogen bulbs,

161
00:06:08,606 --> 00:06:10,572
while using less power.

162
00:06:10,752 --> 00:06:12,636
They need a high voltage pulse to

163
00:06:12,636 --> 00:06:14,405
start, which is why they take a

164
00:06:14,405 --> 00:06:16,232
moment to reach full brightness.

165
00:06:16,412 --> 00:06:18,724
The first car to use them was

166
00:06:18,724 --> 00:06:20,717
the B M W seven series in

167
00:06:20,717 --> 00:06:22,949
the early nineteen nineties.

168
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:25,530
Because they are so bright,

169
00:06:25,530 --> 00:06:28,670
xenon lights are often placed behind a

170
00:06:28,670 --> 00:06:31,892
projector lens, a small glass lens that

171
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:34,536
shapes the beam with a sharp cut

172
00:06:34,536 --> 00:06:35,280
off line.

173
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:38,897
Without it, they would dazzle other drivers.

174
00:06:39,077 --> 00:06:42,439
Fitting xenon bulbs into a reflector made

175
00:06:42,439 --> 00:06:45,227
for halogen, without that control,

176
00:06:45,227 --> 00:06:48,507
is illegal in many countries for exactly

177
00:06:48,507 --> 00:06:49,491
that reason.

178
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:53,242
Why did French cars have yellow headlights?

179
00:06:53,422 --> 00:06:54,978
Because it was the law.

180
00:06:55,158 --> 00:06:57,200
From nineteen thirty-seven,

181
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:00,451
France required headlights to give a yellow

182
00:07:00,451 --> 00:07:00,905
light.

183
00:07:01,085 --> 00:07:03,882
The idea was that yellow light causes

184
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:06,301
less glare for oncoming drivers,

185
00:07:06,301 --> 00:07:08,872
and might cut through fog and rain

186
00:07:08,872 --> 00:07:10,686
better than white light.

187
00:07:11,037 --> 00:07:14,345
Some people also believed it helped identify

188
00:07:14,345 --> 00:07:17,203
French cars, and that the yellow light

189
00:07:17,203 --> 00:07:19,384
was less tiring for the eyes.

190
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,998
The science behind it was never fully

191
00:07:21,998 --> 00:07:22,525
settled.

192
00:07:22,705 --> 00:07:25,348
Yellow light does reduce some glare,

193
00:07:25,348 --> 00:07:28,138
but it also contains less total light.

194
00:07:28,318 --> 00:07:30,544
Drivers saw slightly less,

195
00:07:30,544 --> 00:07:33,798
but others were dazzled a little less.

196
00:07:34,148 --> 00:07:37,069
The rule ended in the nineteen nineties,

197
00:07:37,069 --> 00:07:40,136
when Europe harmonised its rules and white

198
00:07:40,136 --> 00:07:43,203
headlights became the standard everywhere.

199
00:07:43,383 --> 00:07:47,148
Today, yellow headlights are a nostalgic detail,

200
00:07:47,148 --> 00:07:50,207
still fitted by some classic car owners

201
00:07:50,207 --> 00:07:52,561
to make an old French car look

202
00:07:52,561 --> 00:07:53,031
right.

203
00:07:53,211 --> 00:07:56,332
A whole country's night roads were once

204
00:07:56,332 --> 00:07:56,892
yellow.

205
00:07:57,242 --> 00:07:59,865
Why are modern headlights so thin?

206
00:08:00,045 --> 00:08:02,077
Because of LEDs.

207
00:08:02,257 --> 00:08:04,749
A light emitting diode is a tiny

208
00:08:04,749 --> 00:08:08,409
chip that glows when electricity passes through

209
00:08:08,409 --> 00:08:08,643
it.

210
00:08:08,823 --> 00:08:11,267
It is much smaller than a bulb,

211
00:08:11,267 --> 00:08:13,712
so many LEDs can be arranged in

212
00:08:13,712 --> 00:08:15,999
a thin strip or any shape the

213
00:08:15,999 --> 00:08:17,182
designer wants.

214
00:08:17,362 --> 00:08:19,341
Lights can now be just a few

215
00:08:19,341 --> 00:08:20,543
centimetres tall.

216
00:08:20,893 --> 00:08:24,287
LEDs also last much longer than bulbs,

217
00:08:24,287 --> 00:08:27,146
often as long as the car itself,

218
00:08:27,146 --> 00:08:29,379
and they use less energy.

219
00:08:29,559 --> 00:08:31,194
They light up instantly,

220
00:08:31,194 --> 00:08:33,304
and they can be switched on and

221
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:34,462
off very quickly,

222
00:08:34,462 --> 00:08:37,118
which opens the door to smarter lights.

223
00:08:37,298 --> 00:08:40,997
Full LED headlights reached production cars in

224
00:08:40,997 --> 00:08:42,847
the late two thousands.

225
00:08:43,197 --> 00:08:45,372
That is the final answer to why

226
00:08:45,372 --> 00:08:46,285
pop ups died.

227
00:08:46,465 --> 00:08:48,921
A thin LED strip can be placed

228
00:08:48,921 --> 00:08:49,658
in a low,

229
00:08:49,658 --> 00:08:52,605
smooth nose, meet every height rule,

230
00:08:52,605 --> 00:08:54,325
and still look sharp.

231
00:08:54,505 --> 00:08:57,104
The low sports car nose that once

232
00:08:57,104 --> 00:08:59,704
needed pop up lights can now have

233
00:08:59,704 --> 00:09:02,934
permanent ones that are almost invisible.

234
00:09:03,284 --> 00:09:06,642
Why do some headlights have dozens of

235
00:09:06,642 --> 00:09:08,276
small LEDs inside?

236
00:09:08,456 --> 00:09:10,499
They are matrix headlights.

237
00:09:10,679 --> 00:09:14,100
A camera behind the windscreen watches the

238
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:15,730
road for other cars.

239
00:09:15,910 --> 00:09:17,263
When it sees one,

240
00:09:17,263 --> 00:09:20,528
the headlight switches off only the small

241
00:09:20,528 --> 00:09:23,235
LEDs that would shine at that car,

242
00:09:23,235 --> 00:09:26,181
and keeps the high beam on everywhere

243
00:09:26,181 --> 00:09:26,579
else.

244
00:09:26,929 --> 00:09:29,303
The result is a high beam that

245
00:09:29,303 --> 00:09:30,412
never dazzles.

246
00:09:30,592 --> 00:09:33,086
You can drive with full lights all

247
00:09:33,086 --> 00:09:35,507
night, and the system cuts a dark

248
00:09:35,507 --> 00:09:38,589
tunnel around every oncoming car and every

249
00:09:38,589 --> 00:09:39,322
car ahead.

250
00:09:39,502 --> 00:09:41,476
Audi was one of the first to

251
00:09:41,476 --> 00:09:43,591
bring this to production cars,

252
00:09:43,591 --> 00:09:45,354
in the two thousand tens.

253
00:09:45,704 --> 00:09:48,886
The newest systems use thousands or even

254
00:09:48,886 --> 00:09:51,432
more than a million tiny pixels,

255
00:09:51,432 --> 00:09:54,456
and can project symbols onto the road,

256
00:09:54,456 --> 00:09:57,081
like a warning or a guiding line.

257
00:09:57,261 --> 00:09:59,590
The headlight is no longer just a

258
00:09:59,590 --> 00:09:59,943
lamp.

259
00:10:00,123 --> 00:10:01,934
It is a smart projector,

260
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:04,500
guided by a camera and a computer.

261
00:10:04,851 --> 00:10:07,298
Why do some cars have little washers

262
00:10:07,298 --> 00:10:09,065
that spray the headlights?

263
00:10:09,245 --> 00:10:12,097
Because dirt on a bright headlight is

264
00:10:12,097 --> 00:10:12,867
dangerous.

265
00:10:13,047 --> 00:10:15,424
Mud and dust scatter the light in

266
00:10:15,424 --> 00:10:18,522
all directions, instead of keeping it below

267
00:10:18,522 --> 00:10:19,746
the cut off line.

268
00:10:19,926 --> 00:10:23,236
A dirty xenon or LED headlight can

269
00:10:23,236 --> 00:10:27,519
dazzle oncoming drivers even with low beams.

270
00:10:27,870 --> 00:10:29,100
For that reason,

271
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:32,947
European rules have required headlight cleaning on

272
00:10:32,947 --> 00:10:35,562
cars with very powerful low beams,

273
00:10:35,562 --> 00:10:37,332
above a set brightness.

274
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:40,050
The washers are often hidden in the

275
00:10:40,050 --> 00:10:42,371
bumper and pop out when you wash

276
00:10:42,371 --> 00:10:44,764
the windscreen, spraying a short,

277
00:10:44,764 --> 00:10:47,519
strong jet of water at the headlights.

278
00:10:47,870 --> 00:10:50,175
It is a small example of how

279
00:10:50,175 --> 00:10:52,397
one change creates another.

280
00:10:52,577 --> 00:10:55,138
Brighter lights helped drivers see,

281
00:10:55,138 --> 00:10:57,187
but created a glare problem.

282
00:10:57,367 --> 00:10:59,623
The washer is the fix for that

283
00:10:59,623 --> 00:11:00,675
glare problem.

284
00:11:00,855 --> 00:11:04,578
Some modern LED headlights are efficient enough

285
00:11:04,578 --> 00:11:06,004
to avoid the rule,

286
00:11:06,004 --> 00:11:09,331
which is why washers are disappearing too.

287
00:11:09,681 --> 00:11:11,871
Why do cars keep some lights on

288
00:11:11,871 --> 00:11:12,931
during the day?

289
00:11:13,111 --> 00:11:13,831
To be seen.

290
00:11:14,011 --> 00:11:17,443
Daytime running lights make a car easier

291
00:11:17,443 --> 00:11:19,330
to spot from far away,

292
00:11:19,330 --> 00:11:21,646
especially in dull weather,

293
00:11:21,646 --> 00:11:23,276
low sun or shadows.

294
00:11:23,456 --> 00:11:25,248
They are not meant to help the

295
00:11:25,248 --> 00:11:25,906
driver see.

296
00:11:26,086 --> 00:11:28,350
They are meant to help everyone else

297
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:29,104
see the car.

298
00:11:29,455 --> 00:11:31,916
The idea came from Scandinavia,

299
00:11:31,916 --> 00:11:34,853
where winter days are dark and short.

300
00:11:35,033 --> 00:11:38,584
Sweden made daytime lights mandatory in the

301
00:11:38,584 --> 00:11:40,153
nineteen seventies.

302
00:11:40,333 --> 00:11:44,326
The European Union required daytime running lights

303
00:11:44,326 --> 00:11:47,281
on new cars from two thousand eleven,

304
00:11:47,281 --> 00:11:50,875
after studies suggested they help reduce some

305
00:11:50,875 --> 00:11:52,872
types of daytime crashes.

306
00:11:53,222 --> 00:11:56,307
Because daytime lights are always on,

307
00:11:56,307 --> 00:11:58,725
LEDs became perfect for them.

308
00:11:58,905 --> 00:12:01,640
They use little energy and last for

309
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:02,109
years.

310
00:12:02,289 --> 00:12:05,578
Designers then turned them into signatures,

311
00:12:05,578 --> 00:12:09,020
with shapes that make each brand recognisable

312
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,091
from far away.

313
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:13,240
A safety rule became the new face

314
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,230
of the car.

315
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:15,891
So here are the ten.

316
00:12:16,071 --> 00:12:18,123
Pop ups for a low nose and

317
00:12:18,123 --> 00:12:19,148
a height law.

318
00:12:19,328 --> 00:12:22,660
Safety, weight and drag that killed them.

319
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:25,615
Sealed beams that froze design.

320
00:12:25,795 --> 00:12:28,558
Halogen bulbs with a chemical cycle.

321
00:12:28,738 --> 00:12:31,989
Xenon arcs that shine three times brighter.

322
00:12:32,169 --> 00:12:34,328
Yellow lights from a French law.

323
00:12:34,508 --> 00:12:37,852
Thin LEDs that finally solved the problem.

324
00:12:38,032 --> 00:12:40,679
Matrix lights that never dazzle.

325
00:12:40,859 --> 00:12:43,344
Washers that keep them clean.

326
00:12:43,524 --> 00:12:45,946
And daytime lights that help others see

327
00:12:45,946 --> 00:12:46,194
you.

328
00:12:46,544 --> 00:12:49,020
Pop up headlights did not die because

329
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:50,828
people stopped loving them.

330
00:12:51,008 --> 00:12:53,657
They died because the problem they solved

331
00:12:53,657 --> 00:12:54,433
disappeared.

332
00:12:54,613 --> 00:12:57,697
If you want more machines explained part

333
00:12:57,697 --> 00:13:00,627
by part, subscribe to Machine Reverse.

334
00:13:00,807 --> 00:13:02,762
And tell us in the comments which

335
00:13:02,762 --> 00:13:04,835
car with pop ups is your favourite.
